		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5160&amp;p=37611#p37611"><![CDATA[
SUCCESS!<br><br>So, it seems that when I flashed my DM-1701 for OpenGD77, I could not get the flash software to work in Windows 11.<br><br>Rather than debug the problem, I just went to Windows 10 (I am exclusively Mac, but I use Parallels to run Windows 11, 10 and even XP for my wireless radio CPS programming that are not covered by CHIRP)! And it worked perfectly.<br><br>But I forgot this history and all of my failed programming attempts to change the Codeplug were in Windows 11.<br><br>Then I received a reply to one of my Reddit /DMR posts about flashing the DM-1701 for OpenGD77 and the reply reminded me that I had used Windows 10.<br><br>So I just went to my OpenGD77 CPS programming software in Windows 10 and the PAPA System codeplug installed perfectly and works like a charm.<br><br>Thank you to ALL who chimed in on this problem.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1890">W7ML</a> — Mon Jun 30, 2025 8:05 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
