		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5160&amp;p=37363#p37363"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I installed all this last year and it worked well.<br><br>Now I want to give this DM-1701 to our local Repeater group's summer picnic for its fund-raising Raffle.<br><br>In the software, I load NEW and then a more generic codeplug for our groups DMR repeaters (and without my personal information).<br><br>Every time I attempt to write this more generic codeplug into memory over my personal codeplug in memory, it appears to be properly downloading both on the computer and on the DM-1701 screen.<br><br>But my personal codeplug continues to remain in the DM-1701 memory, even when I download it back to the computer.<br><br>Any thoughts?</div></blockquote>Are you sure you are not first reading the old codeplug from the radio and then writing it back<br><br>Try selecting File new in the CPS and simply write that to the radio to start with<br><br>Btw.<br><br>Make sure you only have one radio connected to your PC at the time.  If you have multiple radios connected the CPS does not check for this and may be uploading to the other radio<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Tue Jun 03, 2025 9:23 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
